From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:58:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] nvk/android: render swapchain images in VRAM by default

Measured on the G14 (RTX 5070 Ti Laptop, window buffers linear in system
memory for the Radeon): GPU Check's full-window ALU shader 510 fps with
VRAM swapchain images against 361 rendering into the window buffer (the
Radeon 890M: 377-393), its clear-only frames 950-979 fps against 375-777;
three apps (Photos, Kindle, Plex), two runs each in alternating order,
within run-to-run noise of the old path; the RTX still reaches D3cold
with such an app in the background.  NVK_ANB_VRAM=0 restores 0037's
direct rendering.

ANAL-309 (GoodBook).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
index 6a01d26..1a5b9a4 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
@@ -1695,13 +1695,13 @@ nvk_create_drm_physical_device(struct vk_instance *_instance,
    /* On a hybrid laptop the window buffer is linear system memory, which the
     * other GPU scans out; rendering into it sends every pixel write and blend
     * read over PCIe, and with a depth/stencil attachment NVK copies it in and
-    * out of a tiled shadow at every render pass.  NVK_ANB_VRAM=1 (on Android
-    * also debug.mesa.nvk.anb.vram) renders swapchain images in VRAM and copies
-    * each frame into its window buffer once, in the release submission (so
-    * only with the release fence).
+    * out of a tiled shadow at every render pass.  So swapchain images are
+    * rendered in VRAM and each frame is copied into its window buffer once, in
+    * the release submission (so only with the release fence).  NVK_ANB_VRAM=0
+    * (on Android also debug.mesa.nvk.anb.vram) renders into the window buffer.
     */
    pdev->anb_vram = pdev->anb_release_fence &&
-                    debug_get_bool_option("NVK_ANB_VRAM", false);
+                    debug_get_bool_option("NVK_ANB_VRAM", true);
 #endif
 
    pdev->nak = nak_compiler_create(&pdev->info);
